{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=law",{"First week of July I wrote eleven speeding tickets, seems like somebody else's life","I worked the county fair every August, lost kids and drunks - Lord, I miss lost kids and drunks","Sheriff used to say the job's ninety percent paperwork, I'd give a lot for some paperwork","Dispatch log from the ninth says 'disturbance, subject biting.' We all laughed at that one","My wife packed my lunch every shift, bologna, every day - never once told her I hated bologna","Used to know every family on my side of the county by their dog's name","The jail in West Point is overrun, last I heard, nobody's alive","Roadblock on Highway 31 fell on the fifth, deputies fell back"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=swat",{"Our team trained twice a month, never once on anything like this","Last real call-out was a barricaded drunk in Valley Station - he gave up when his mother showed up","Range day was every other Tuesday, coffee and donuts after - seems silly to miss it","We used to grumble about the overtime, now it's all overtime","Best call I ever had was a cat stuck behind a water heater - took four of us","Mall's a deathtrap - don't bother"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=swat|world=vehicle",{"I kept my kit in the trunk, ready to go - still do - habit"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=military,elite",{"We were supposed to be on two weeks of annual training - that was in June","I joined the Guard for college money, funny how that worked out","Sergeant Boyd used to say a clean rifle is a happy rifle - he kept his clean right to the end","My unit did flood relief in '91, sandbags for a week, I thought that was hard","Mail call was the best part of the day, haven't had mail in weeks","Last rumor I heard, it all started at some lab up near Louisville - week before, it was a meteor","Stationed near here, did my training at the post, this place was alive then","Went to a bar in that town on leave, great place, great people, shame"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=civilian,family,worker,rescue",{"I keep reaching for the light switch when I walk in a room - every time","We had tickets for that dinosaur picture Saturday night, never did get to see it","My boss docked me an hour for being late on the eighth - I hope he's alright, I really do","Used to drive to Louisville for the mall, driving somewhere just to walk around - can you imagine?"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=civilian,family,worker,rescue|world=road",{"Sunday mornings Mama made biscuits and the whole street could smell 'em","I left the sprinkler running when we went - Lawn's probably the only green thing left on our street"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=raider,outlaw,gang,club,crime,prison",{"Had a court date on the twelfth, guess I'm a free man","Used to work the line at the plant, hated every minute, miss the paycheck though","My old lady threw me out in June, turns out that was the best thing ever happened to her","My probation officer had a mustache like a push broom - I think about that guy a lot"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=raider,outlaw,gang,club,crime,prison|world=road",{"Ran a card game out of the back of the bowling alley - good money - real chairs"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=raider,outlaw,gang,club,crime,prison|world=vehicle,water",{"I stole a car once just to drive up to Indiana and see a lake - wasn't even a nice lake"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=civilian",{"They say Muldraugh was the first to fall, I don't know if that's true","I heard a lady in Riverside holed up in a bank vault for a week","Somebody said the mall in Louisville is full of them"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=family",{"My sister called from West Point before the phones died - she sounded scared","The church bell in Riverside used to ring every Sunday - now it's silent"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=worker",{"Plant in Muldraugh went dark Friday, half the shift never made it home"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=worker|world=cars",{"Trucks stopped coming through Ekron, nobody knows why"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=rescue",{"Firehouse in Rosewood caught fire last week, nobody got out - I think","Hospital in Louisville stopped taking patients - doctors left","I did my clinical rotation at that hospital, long nights, bad coffee","Walked this block a thousand times with a stethoscope around my neck"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=military",{"The cordon around Muldraugh fell Tuesday - reports vary","Convoy was ambushed outside Brandenburg, nobody came back"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=elite",{"Muldraugh checkpoint is compromised - avoid"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=outlaw",{"Heard there's a man in Irvington paying for fuel, could be a trap","Some outfit took over the gas station in Ekron, they charge a toll"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=raider|world=road",{"Word is there's a convoy full of food out on the highway"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=raider",{"Rosewood's easy pickings, nobody's left to guard it"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=gang",{"Louisville's a mess, whole block's burned, we got out"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=gang|world=water,road",{"Another crew's moving in on the river road, we'll handle it"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=club|world=road",{"Roads out of Fallas Lake are clear - mostly"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=club",{"Heard the Rosewood clubhouse got overrun, good men lost"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=crime",{"Somebody's buying fuel in Muldraugh, offering good money","The warehouse in West Point has supplies, and a very nervous owner"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=prison",{"Heard the state pen is wide open, whole wing walked out","Heard there's a bounty on escapees - keep your head down"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","",{"This used to be the best barbecue in the county","Places like this remind me of my first kiss","We used to hang out right there, every Friday night","They had a jukebox in that diner, remember the jukebox?","I remember buying my first car. Thought I knew everything","That's where I learned to drive, in that parking lot, Dad yelling","I came to this very spot on prom night, believe it or not","The old movie theater, two bucks on Tuesdays, can you believe it","I played Little League in that field, left field, never caught a ball","There was a candy store on the corner, penny candy, honest to God","We used to jump off that bridge, in the summer, all of us","My grandmother lived two houses down, I used to walk over for pie","My first job was right there, bagging groceries, minimum wage","We got married in that church, that one right there, with the white steeple","I used to buy bait every Saturday. Just a habit","Everybody went to that skating rink, every birthday, every single one"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=civilian,family,worker|tmp=fresh|mood=sad",{"I can't walk through this town without seeing everybody who used to live in it","That was Mr Hadley's place, he waved at everybody, every morning, everybody","I never thought I'd see this street without people on it","Class of eighty-nine, we all hung out right here, where are they now","That's where we had our graduation party, my whole family, my whole life"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=civilian,family,worker|tmp=fresh|mood=warm",{"Strawberry festival, every June, the whole town came out, the whole TOWN","Parade on Main Street, tractors and clowns and the high school band, I loved it","County fair, ferris wheel, they had one, rusty, but it spun"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=civilian,family,worker|tmp=seasoned|mood=calm",{"Every place has its ghost, you just have to listen","I know these roads like the back of my hand, which isn't saying much anymore","Places don't forget, people do"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=civilian,family,worker|tmp=seasoned|mood=funny",{"Back then you could get a milkshake and a burger for under three bucks, heh","Used to complain about the traffic on this road, listen to me now"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","role=rescue_clergy",{"I baptized half the kids in this town right there, in that little creek"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","role=rescue_firefighter",{"We put out a grease fire at that diner back in eighty-seven, free pie for a month"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=law,swat",{"I pulled over half this town on this road, nicest folks you'd meet","Wrote a ticket in that lot, to my own cousin, family never forgave me","Used to be you knew every house, every dog, every family, every problem"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=law,swat|tmp=veteran",{"This used to be a quiet beat, now look at it"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=military,elite|tmp=veteran|mood=calm",{"You see a place once, you remember it forever, see it twice, you forget it"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=outlaw,raider,gang,club,crime,prison",{"I knew a guy who lived on that block, owed me forty bucks","Spent a night in that jail, it wasn't so bad, bad coffee","I lifted a bike from that yard when I was twelve, still feel bad about it","There was a pool hall there, my daddy won it in a card game, lost it in another"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","reg=outlaw,raider,gang,club,crime,prison|mood=sad",{"I grew up three streets from here, it's gone, it's all gone"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","hour=5,8",{"Morning light hits this block just right, always did"}},
{"LOCAL_MEMORY","hour=17,20",{"Used to be the lights would come on about now, house by house"}},
